<title>GREECE: Greek closed-end funds NAV drops in June.</title>
<headline>Greek closed-end funds NAV drops in June.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's 16 closed-end investment funds listed on the Athens bourse had a market capitalisation of 155.8 billion drachmas at the end of the first half, down 15 percent from 183.3 billion in May, the Association of Institutional Investors said.</p>
<p>Statistics showed that only three out of 16 funds were trading at a premium to their net asset value (NAV) at the end of June.</p>
<p>Only two funds managed to outperform the market's 59.08 percent return in the first half -- National Invest and Aeolian Fund.</p>
<p>Total NAV amounted to 166.3 billion drachmas versus 170.7 billion at the end of May.</p>
<p>Closed-end funds traded at an average 6.3 percent discount to total capitalisation at end-June, the association said. They had traded at a 7.4 percent premium a month earlier.</p>
<p>The funds made few changes to their equity allocations during June, but had switched funds from fixed income securities to cash instruments.</p>
